.TH JSON 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Json \- JSON serialisation and deserialisation
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Json
module provides JSON parsing, serialisation, and validation using the
nlohmann/json C++ library.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS ParseJson
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
any() ParseJson(jsonString: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Parses
.I jsonString
as JSON and returns a y-- value tree.
Mapping: null->none, bool->bool, integer->int, float->float,
string->string, array->list, object->instance (fields = JSON keys).
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR, \fBParseError\fR (with byte offset)
.SS StringifyJson
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
string() StringifyJson(value: any(), indent: int() = -1)
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Serialises
.I value
to a JSON string.
Cyclic references are replaced with "[Cyclic Reference]".
Indent -1 (default) = compact; positive = pretty-printed.
Unsupported field types in instances are silently skipped.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR
.SS IsValidJson
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
bool() IsValidJson(jsonString: string())
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Returns true if
.I jsonString
is valid JSON.  Does not throw on invalid input.
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBArgumentError\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
Regex(3), Http(3)
